          "output": "<p>Title: Factura electrónica obligatoria 2026 — Facturi</p>\n<p>The <strong>factura electrónica obligatoria</strong> mandated by the <strong>Ley Crea y Crece</strong> and Real Decreto 238/2026 establishes a standardized digital billing system for B2B transactions in Spain. Its primary goals include reducing commercial delinquency through automated payment tracking and enhancing tax transparency. Companies must transition from traditional PDFs to structured formats, such as XML, that facilitate automatic processing between business systems. The implementation follows a staggered timeline contingent upon the upcoming publication of a ministerial order. Large enterprises with over 8 million euros in revenue must comply within 12 months of this order, while smaller businesses and autonomous workers are granted a 24-month adaptation period. To ensure interoperability, the system will allow the use of private platforms alongside a free public solution provided by the Agencia Tributaria. Businesses should prepare by adopting professional invoicing software and digitizing their records to meet these technical requirements without disruption.</p>",
